    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait what do you mean by a goblin's whisper? what does that have to do with my ac unit? i'm just trying to figure out if it's a blown capacitor or something like that.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A goblin's whisper is just a colloquialism I like to use to describe a faint, mysterious noise that's not quite loud enough to be alarming, but still suspicious. It's like the sound of a goblin whispering in the darkness, trying to get your attention without being too obvious.\n\nNow, back to your AC unit. A blown capacitor is definitely a possibility, especially if the humming noise is accompanied by a flickering or dimming of the unit's lights. You might want to check the capacitor first, but be careful not to touch any electrical components if you're not familiar with the unit's wiring.\n\nAnother possibility is a faulty contactor or a malfunctioning relay. These components can cause the compressor to hum or whine, even if the blades aren't spinning. It's a bit like a goblin trying to sneak into the AC unit's control room without being detected - it's a sneaky, stealthy operation.\n\nIf you're still unsure, you can try to listen more closely to the humming noise. Is it a steady, constant hum, or does it vary in pitch or volume? This might give you a clue about what's going on inside the unit.",
